From: Jan Catrysse <jan.catrysse@geoxyz.eu>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:27:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Do not look up 'is there any workflow' per saved record
 (2.1.3, Redmine 5.1)

Same change as 619d66d on redmine70-migration, for the code production runs
(0398974, plugin 2.1.3 on Redmine 5.1). Adding a group of 1000 users to a
project asked the database per member whether any member workflow or shared
code exists. CustomWorkflow.active_observable? answers it once per request or
job (RedmineCustomWorkflows::Current), at most a minute in other processes,
and forgets it when a workflow is saved or destroyed.

Measured on Redmine 5.1-stable-GEOxyz (bcf917c), PostgreSQL 16, only an issue
workflow active, group of 1000 users added to a project (rolled back): 11,010
-> 8,008 queries (custom_workflows 3,003 -> 1), 9.7 s -> 6.3 s.

Tests: test/unit/workflow_lookup_test.rb (12 vs 24 custom_workflows queries
for 2 and 4 member saves without the change, equal with it; workflows added
after a first save still run). Suite: 68 runs, 112 assertions, 0 failures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UqNczmW8rty27YMoNMW8iq
